{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"28":"Foods (Kitab Al-At'imah)"},"section_detail":{"28":{"hadithnumber_first":3736,"hadithnumber_last":3854,"arabicnumber_first":3736,"arabicnumber_last":3854,"name_native":"Foods (Kitab Al-At'imah)"}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":3791,"arabicnumber":3791,"text":"Anas b. Malik said:I was an adolescent boy. I hunted a hare and roasted it. Abu Talha sent its hunch through me to the Prophet (ﷺ), so I brought it to him and he accepted it","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Sahih"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Sahih Bukhari (2572) Sahih Muslim (1953)"}],"reference":{"book":28,"hadith":56}}]}